th="2089" data-file-height="3704" data-file-type="bitmap" height="296" width="167" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:169px;max-width:169px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:295px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Celtics_at_Wizards_2024-12-015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1639" data-file-height="2896" data-file-type="bitmap" height="295" width="167" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div></div></div><div class="trow" style="display:flex"><div class="thumbcaption"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayson_Tatum" title="Jayson Tatum">Jayson Tatum</a> (left) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaylen_Brown" title="Jaylen Brown">Jaylen Brown</a> (right) scored 31 and 30 points respectively to secure a 3–0 series lead for the Celtics.</div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt200"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"/></span>
<p id="mwAno">Jayson Tatum and Jaylen Brown scored 31 and 30 points to stave off a late-game Mavericks rally and put the Celtics up 3–0 in the series.<sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:142_42-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":142"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:142-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:142-42" id="mwAns"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn0">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn4">]</span></span></a></sup> It was the second time in franchise history that two players each scored 30-plus points in a Finals game.<sup about="#mwt207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAn8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoE">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">]</span></span></a></sup> Tatum logged six rebounds and five assists while Brown had eight rebounds and eight assists,<sup about="#mwt210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:152_44-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":152"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:152-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:152-44" id="mwAoM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoU">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoY">]</span></span></a></sup> with the victory extending Boston's playoff winning-streak to 10 and its road-game winning-streak to seven. The only other Celtic to score in double-figures was Derrick White, who had 16 points.<sup about="#mwt213" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:162_45-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":162"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:162-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:162-45" id="mwAoc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAog"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAok">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoo">]</span></span></a></sup> Kyrie Irving led all scorers with 35 points, while Luka Dončić had 27 points, six rebounds and six assists.<sup about="#mwt216" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:172_46-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":172"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:172-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:172-46" id="mwAos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo4">]</span></span></a></sup> Coming into the game, the Celtics were without the injured Kristaps Porziņģis,<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:162_45-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":162"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:162-45" id="mwAo8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApE">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApI">]</span></span></a></sup> who was replaced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Horford" title="Al Horford" id="mwApM">Al Horford</a> and occasionally <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Tillman" title="Xavier Tillman" id="mwApQ">Xavier Tillman</a> at the center position. The Mavericks, specifically Irving and Dončić, took advantage of the lack of size for Boston to attack the rim,<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:182_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":182"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:182-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:182-47" id="mwApU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApc">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApg">]</span></span></a></sup> outscoring Boston 52–36 from the area during the game.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:192_48-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":192"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:192-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:192-48" id="mwApk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAps">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAp0">The Mavericks started strong, scoring nine points to force a timeout from the Celtics early on.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:182_47-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:182-47" id="mwAp4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAp8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqA">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqE">]</span></span></a></sup> The Mavericks heavily utilized the paint<sup about="#mwt225" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:192_48-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":192"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:192-48" id="mwAqI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqQ">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqU">]</span></span></a></sup> to outscore the Celtics 22–9 by the midpoint of the quarter—their largest lead in the series by that point. The Celtics responded with a 21–9 run led by Brown and Tatum.<sup about="#mwt226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:142_42-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:142-42" id="mwAqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqg">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:182_47-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:182-47" id="mwAqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqw">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq0">]</span></span></a></sup> The second quarter was defense-oriented at first, with the Celtics leading the scoring 5–2 at the halfway mark before Irving and Tatum began responding to each other's three-pointers,<sup about="#mwt228" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:142_42-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:142-42" id="mwAq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArE">]</span></span></a></sup> ending the half at a near tie.<sup about="#mwt229" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:152_44-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":152"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:152-44" id="mwArI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArU">]</span></span></a></sup> The Celtics dominated the third quarter, scoring on their first seven possessions to establish an imposing lead as Brown scored half of his points in the game during the timeframe.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:182_47-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:182-47" id="mwArY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArg">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArk">]</span></span></a></sup> After Dončić made a layup to bring the lead down to six with 5:11 remaining, the Celtics went on a 7–0 run to end the quarter with a 15-point lead, outscoring the Mavericks 35–19 in total.<sup about="#mwt231" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:172_46-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:172-46" id="mwAro"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArw">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAr4">Up until the final quarter, the Mavericks, excluding Irving and Dončić, combined for only 19 points.<sup about="#mwt234" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAr8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsE">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsI">]</span></span></a></sup> The Celtics initially continued their offensive momentum into the fourth quarter, capitalized by a three-pointer from White a minute in to extend the lead to 21 points.<sup about="#mwt235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:172_46-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:172-46" id="mwAsM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsU">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the Mavericks proceeded to go on a 22–2 run, with contributions from P. J. Washington and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dereck_Lively_II" title="Dereck Lively II" id="mwAsc">Dereck Lively II</a>,<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:192_48-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":192"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:192-48" id="mwAsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAso">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAss">]</span></span></a></sup> cutting the deficit to 93–90. During this stretch, Dončić fouled out with 4:12 remaining.<sup about="#mwt237" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:142_42-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:142-42" id="mwAsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs4">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs8">]</span></span></a></sup> Lively later scored a dunk to put the Celtics lead at 100–98 until Brown hit a mid-range jump shot with 1:01 left.<sup about="#mwt238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:172_46-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:172-46" id="mwAtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtI">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtM">]</span></span></a></sup> Sam Quinn of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBS_Sports" title="CBS Sports" id="mwAtQ">CBS Sports</a> retrospectively viewed Brown's shot as "the dagger that won that contest for Boston."<sup about="#mwt241" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-50" id="mwAtU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtc">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtg">]</span></span></a></sup> From there, Washington, Irving, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Hardaway_Jr." title="Tim Hardaway Jr." id="mwAtk">Tim Hardaway Jr.</a> each missed their three-point attempts as a foul on Tatum with 14.6 seconds left allowed him to make free throws to secure the game and preventing what would have tied the largest comeback from a fourth-quarter deficit in NBA history.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:162_45-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":162"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:162-45" id="mwAto"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAts"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtw">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt0">]</span></span></a></sup></p><p id="mwAt4">

As was done for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Walton" title="Bill Walton" id="mwAt8">Bill Walton</a> prior to Game 1, a moment of silence was held before the game for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_West" title="Jerry West" id="mwAuA">Jerry West</a>, who died earlier that same day at the age of 86. West's silhouette was the basis for the NBA logo, and he was an NBA champion as a player in 1972 with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Lakers" title="Los Angeles Lakers" id="mwAuE">Los Angeles Lakers</a> and also a further eight times as an executive with the Lakers and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_State_Warriors" title="Golden State Warriors" id="mwAuI">Golden State Warriors</a>.<sup about="#mwt247" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAuM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuU">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt250" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-52" id="mwAuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuk">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuo">]</span></span></a></sup></p><div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt243" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAus" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clear","href":"./Template:Clear"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAuw" aria-labelledby="Game_4"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_4">Game 4</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2024_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Game 4"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
