</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAu8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Luka_Dončić_2021.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAvA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Luka_Dončić_2021.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Luka_Don%C4%8Di%C4%87_2021.jpg/250px-Luka_Don%C4%8Di%C4%87_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Luka_Don%C4%8Di%C4%87_2021.jpg/500px-Luka_Don%C4%8Di%C4%87_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Image of Luka Dončić in a Mavericks uniform in a basketball game." data-file-width="1203" data-file-height="1618" data-file-type="bitmap" height="269" width="200" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAvE"/></a><figcaption id="mwAvI">A blowout Mavericks victory spearheaded by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luka_Dončić" title="Luka Dončić" id="mwAvM">Luka Dončić</a>'s 29 points prevented a series sweep by the Celtics.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAvQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2024_NBA_Finals_–_Game_4.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAvU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2024_NBA_Finals_–_Game_4.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/2024_NBA_Finals_%E2%80%93_Game_4.png/250px-2024_NBA_Finals_%E2%80%93_Game_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/2024_NBA_Finals_%E2%80%93_Game_4.png/500px-2024_NBA_Finals_%E2%80%93_Game_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1920" data-file-height="1080" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAvY"/></a><figcaption id="mwAvc">A timeout during Game 4</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAvg">The Mavericks avoided a sweep by the Celtics with a 122–84 blowout victory—the third largest in NBA Finals history—to cut Boston's series lead to 3–1.<sup about="#mwt254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-53" id="mwAvk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvs">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvw">]</span></span></a></sup> Luka Dončić led Dallas with 29 points, five rebounds, five assists and three steals. He scored 25 of his total points in the first two quarters, the most ever recorded by a Maverick in a Finals game by halftime.<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwAv0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAv4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv8">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwA">]</span></span></a></sup> Kyrie Irving had 21 points and six assists,<sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_55-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-55" id="mwAwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwM">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and Tim Hardaway Jr. had 15 points off five three-pointers in the fourth quarter, becoming the third player to have scored five threes in a single quarter of a Finals game.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwc">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwg">]</span></span></a></sup> Dereck Lively II had 11 points and 12 rebounds, becoming the second player to achieve multiple double-doubles in the Finals at the age of 20.<sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:3-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-57" id="mwAwk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAws">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAww">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAw0">Midway through the first quarter, Lively scored his first career three-pointer which gave the Mavericks the lead for the rest of the game.<sup about="#mwt267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_53-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-53" id="mwAw4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAw8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxA">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxE">]</span></span></a></sup> The Mavericks established a 13-point lead by the end of the first,<sup about="#mwt270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAxI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxQ">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxU">]</span></span></a></sup> and a 26-point lead by the half,<sup about="#mwt271" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_53-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-53" id="mwAxY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxg">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxk">]</span></span></a></sup> the fourth largest in Finals history.<sup about="#mwt272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_57-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-57" id="mwAxo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxw">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAx0">]</span></span></a></sup> At halftime, the only Celtics players who made more than one field goal were Jayson Tatum and Jaylen Brown.<sup about="#mwt273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_55-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-55" id="mwAx4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAx8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyA">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyE">]</span></span></a></sup> The Mavericks continued their momentum into the third quarter, outscoring the Celtics by 15–7 points within the first 4:32. With 3:18 left in the third quarter and the deficit at 36 points, the Celtics ceded defeat by substituting out his starters, which was soon followed by the Mavericks doing the same.<sup about="#mwt274" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_57-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-57" id="mwAyI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyQ">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyU">]</span></span></a></sup></p><p id="mwAyY">

It was the Celtics' largest defeat of the season and their worst overall since the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_NBA_playoffs#Eastern_Conference_finals" title="2017 NBA playoffs" id="mwAyc">2017 Eastern Conference Finals</a>.<sup about="#mwt276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_55-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-55" id="mwAyg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyo">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAys">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt279" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ESPNG5_59-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ESPNG5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ESPNG5-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ESPNG5-59" id="mwAyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAy4">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAy8">]</span></span></a></sup> It ended a 10-game postseason winning streak and seven-game road streak, and avoided the chance of them becoming the first team in NBA history to sweep both the Conference Finals and the Finals.<sup about="#mwt280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_53-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-53" id="mwAzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzI">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzM">]</span></span></a></sup> The 84 points they scored was the lowest tally of the season,<sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_57-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-57" id="mwAzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzY">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzc">]</span></span></a></sup> while the game-high 48 points the Mavericks led by was their largest deficit. The 35 points they scored by half was their lowest in two seasons, and the second lowest in a Finals game in franchise history. Tatum and Brown finished with 15 and 10 points respectively.<sup about="#mwt282" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_53-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-53" id="mwAzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzo">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzs">]</span></span></a></sup></p><div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt275" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAzw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clear","href":"./Template:Clear"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAz0" aria-labelledby="Game_5"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_5">Game 5</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2024_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Game 5"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt283" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAz4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"June 17"},"time":{"wt":"8:30 pm"},"place":{"wt":"[[TD Garden]], [[Boston, Massachusetts]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"[[Dallas Mavericks]]"},"score1":{"wt":"88"},"team2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Boston Celtics]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;106&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/dal-vs-bos-0042300405 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"18–&apos;&apos;&apos;28&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q2":{"wt":"28–&apos;&apos;&apos;39&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q3":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;21&apos;&apos;&apos;–19"},"Q4":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;21&apos;&apos;&apos;–20"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Luka Dončić]] 28"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Jayson Tatum]] 31"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"Luka Dončić 12"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"[[Jrue Holiday]] 11"},"assist1":{"wt":"[[Kyrie Irving]] 9"},"assist2":{"wt":"Jayson Tatum 11"},"attendance":{"wt":"19,156"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 15 [[Zach Zarba]]\n*No. 10 John Goble\n*No. 55 [[Bill Kennedy (referee)|Bill Kennedy]]"},"series":{"wt":"Boston wins NBA Finals, 4–1"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt283" id="mwAz8">
