<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="text-align:center">June 17<br/><small> 8:30 pm</small></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:left; width:7%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nba.com/game/dal-vs-bos-0042300405" class="external text">Recap</a></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:left; width:50%; text-align:center">
<tbody><tr style="vertical-align:top">
<td colspan="3" style="text-align:center; border-style:none"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas_Mavericks" title="Dallas Mavericks">Dallas Mavericks</a> 88, <b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Celtics" title="Boston Celtics">Boston Celtics</a></b> <b>106</b>
</td></tr>
<tr style="vertical-align:top; font-size:85%"><td style="text-align:center; border-style:none" colspan="3"><b>Scoring by quarter:</b> 18–<b>28</b>, 28–<b>39</b>, <b>21</b>–19, <b>21</b>–20</td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top; font-size:85%">
<td style="width:48%; text-align:right; border-style:none"><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_(basketball)" title="Point (basketball)" class="mw-redirect">Pts</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luka_Dončić" title="Luka Dončić">Luka Dončić</a> 28<br/><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebound_(basketball)" title="Rebound (basketball)">Rebs</a>:</b> Luka Dončić 12<br/><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assist_(basketball)" title="Assist (basketball)">Asts</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyrie_Irving" title="Kyrie Irving">Kyrie Irving</a> 9</td>
<td></td>
<td style="width:48%; text-align:left; border-style:none"><b>Pts:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayson_Tatum" title="Jayson Tatum">Jayson Tatum</a> 31<br/><b>Rebs:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jrue_Holiday" title="Jrue Holiday">Jrue Holiday</a> 11<br/><b>Asts:</b> Jayson Tatum 11</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="text-align:center; border-style:none"><i><b>Boston wins NBA Finals, 4–1</b></i></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:right; width:24%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TD_Garden" title="TD Garden">TD Garden</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston,_Massachusetts" title="Boston, Massachusetts" class="mw-redirect">Boston, Massachusetts</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 19,156<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 15 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Zarba" title="Zach Zarba">Zach Zarba</a></li>
<li>No. 10 John Goble</li>
<li>No. 55 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Kennedy_(referee)" title="Bill Kennedy (referee)">Bill Kennedy</a></li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA0A"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA0E"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg/250px-Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg/500px-Jaylen_Brown_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Image of Jaylen Brown in a Celtics uniform in a basketball game attempting a jump shot." data-file-width="1497" data-file-height="2535" data-file-type="bitmap" height="339" width="200" class="mw-file-element" id="mwA0I"/></a><figcaption id="mwA0M"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaylen_Brown" title="Jaylen Brown" id="mwA0Q">Jaylen Brown</a> was awarded <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_award" title="NBA Finals Most Valuable Player award" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA0U">Finals MVP</a> after averaging 20.8 points, 5.4 rebounds, and 5 assists per game in the series.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwA0Y">The Celtics closed out the series in a dominant 106–88 victory at home to claim the NBA championship. Jayson Tatum led them to victory with 31 points, eight rebounds and 11 assists, while Jaylen Brown had 21 points, eight rebounds and six assists.<sup about="#mwt286" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:16_60-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":16"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:16-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:16-60" id="mwA0c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0k">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0o">]</span></span></a></sup> Jrue Holiday, who had 14 points and 11 rebounds,<sup about="#mwt287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:16_60-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:16-60" id="mwA0s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA00">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA04">]</span></span></a></sup> scored the first three field goals of the game for the Celtics.<sup about="#mwt290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YahooG5_61-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"YahooG5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-YahooG5-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-YahooG5-61" id="mwA08"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1E">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1I">]</span></span></a></sup> Playing through an injury that he suffered in Game 2 and sidelined him in Games 3 and 4, Kristaps Porziņģis checked in midway through the first quarter to a standing ovation. He finished with five points in 16 minutes.<sup about="#mwt293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwA1M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1U">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwA1c">The Mavericks managed to cut the lead to a single point midway through the first quarter, but the Celtics responded with a 12–3 run powered by eight points between Tatum and Brown. Dallas once again attempted a comeback in the second quarter by bringing a 15-point lead down to nine, but Boston proceeded to outscore them 19–7.<sup about="#mwt294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:16_60-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:16-60" id="mwA1g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1o">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1s">]</span></span></a></sup> The Celtics finished the first half with a 21-point lead, which culminated with Payton Pritchard's buzzer-beating half-court shot, the longest made field goal in the Finals since at least 1998.<sup about="#mwt297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwA1w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA10"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA14">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA18">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt300" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:17_64-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":17"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:17-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:17-64" id="mwA2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2I">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2M">]</span></span></a></sup> The Mavericks never recovered or led at any point during the game, with the Celtics extending their lead to as much as 26 points in the third quarter.<sup about="#mwt301" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:17_64-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:17-64" id="mwA2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2Y">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2c">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwA2g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahoo_Sports" title="Yahoo Sports" id="mwA2k">Yahoo Sports</a></i> dubbed the fourth quarter a "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation" title="Coronation" id="mwA2o">coronation</a>" for the Celtics.<sup about="#mwt302" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YahooG5_61-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"YahooG5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-YahooG5-61" id="mwA2s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA20">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA24">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA28">Luka Dončić led the Mavericks with 28 points, 12 rebounds, five assists, and three steals. He missed his first six three-pointers and finished 2 of 9 from that range. Further noted was his poor defensive performance and his seven turnovers.<sup about="#mwt303" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YahooG5_61-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"YahooG5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-YahooG5-61" id="mwA3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3I">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt306" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwA3Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3Y">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3c">]</span></span></a></sup> Nonetheless, he ended the series averaging 29.2 points, 8.8 rebounds and 5.6 assists, leading all players in points per game.<sup about="#mwt309" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:24_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":24"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:24-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:24-66" id="mwA3g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3o">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3s">]</span></span></a></sup> Similar to the first two games, Kyrie Irving struggled and finished with 15 points on 5 of 16 shooting. With Dončić and Irving struggling early the Mavericks had no response.<sup about="#mwt310" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:17_64-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:17-64" id="mwA3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA30"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA34">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA38">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt311" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YahooG5_61-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"YahooG5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-YahooG5-61" id="mwA4A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4I">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4M">]</span></span></a></sup> The Celtics had a 51–35 rebounding advantage and went 17 of 20 (85%) on their free throws line compared to the Mavericks' 7 of 13 (53.8%).<sup about="#mwt312" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YahooG5_61-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"YahooG5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-YahooG5-61" id="mwA4Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4Y">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4c">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA4g">With the conclusion of the Finals, Brown was named the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player" title="NBA Finals Most Valuable Player" id="mwA4k">NBA Finals Most Valuable Player</a> after averaging 20.8 points, 5.4 rebounds, and 5.0 assists per game. This was in spite of Tatum, generally considered the best player on the Celtics,<sup about="#mwt313" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_50-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-50" id="mwA4o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4w">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA40">]</span></span></a></sup> leading him in most statistical categories with 22.2 points, 7.8 rebounds, and 7.2 assists per game.<sup about="#mwt316" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:25_67-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":25"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:25-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:25-67" id="mwA44"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA48"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5A">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5E">]</span></span></a></sup> Brown's performance as the primary defender on Dončić was regarded as a major factor in the series, as he limited his three-point shooting to 24.4% and significantly inhibited his playmaking, with his assists dropping from 9.8 per game in the regular season.<sup about="#mwt317" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:24_66-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:24-66" id="mwA5I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5Q">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5U">]</span></span></a></sup> Brown also had a higher field goal percentage (44%) compared to Tatum (38.8%) and made important shots throughout the series.<sup about="#mwt318" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:25_67-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:25-67" id="mwA5Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5g">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt319" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_50-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-50" id="mwA5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5w">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA50">]</span></span></a></sup> Both Brown and Tatum said the winner of the award did not matter to them as their goal was to win the championship, each emphasizing each other's and the team's accomplishment.<sup about="#mwt320" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:24_66-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:24-66" id="mwA54"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA58"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6A">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwA6I" aria-labelledby="Rosters"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Rosters">Rosters</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2024_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Rosters"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
